    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0721" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2895</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Magruder</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 659</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 24</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on July
                    23, 1916, the Governments of Denmark, Norway, and Sweden telegraphically
                    instructed <pb facs="0722" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/> their respective
                    representatives at London and Paris simultaneously to present a formal
                    reservation of rights, by means of identic notes, in respect of the action taken
                    by the British and French Governments in declaring the Declaration of London to
                    be null and void. The text of the reservation presented to the British
                    Government (together with a translation thereof) is herewith enclosed.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d541-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Swedish Ministry of Foreign Affairs informs me that the Swedish Minister at
                    Washington has been telegraphically instructed to bring to the attention of the
                    United States Government the joint action of Denmark, Norway, and Sweden herein
                    reported, and earnestly to urge the United States to take similar action in the
                    premises.</p>
                <p>The Spanish Minister at Stockholm has already informed the Swedish Government
                    that he is in receipt of a telegraphic instruction from his Government to the
                    effect that the Spanish Ministers at London and Paris have been directed to make
                    formal reservations analogous to those made by the Scandinavian
                    representatives.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander R. Magruder</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
